    "title": "No 16-year-old in goal! - Confirmed UCL lineups: FC Bayern Munich vs. Atalanta Bergamo - Yahoo Sports",
    "text": "AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementTRENDINGYankees shut out GiantsJudge's golden sombreroSign up for fantasy baseballOpening day starting pitchersSweet 16 previewStory byNo 16-year-old in goal! - Confirmed UCL lineups: FC Bayern Munich vs. Atalanta BergamoBulinewsWed, Mar 18, 2026·1 min readAdd Yahoo Sports on GoogleSpeculation had been building, but now it’s official: there will be no surprise in goal for Bayern Munich against Atalanta Bergamo, as Jonas Urbig has recovered in time to start between the sticks.Following injuries to Manuel Neuer a few weeks ago, Sven Ulreich on Saturday, and Urbig himself last week, many had expected 16-year-old prodigy Leonard Prescott to make his professional debut.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAtalanta face a daunting task, with Bayern holding a commanding 6-1 advantage from the first leg. With just under an hour until kick-off, here are the confirmed lineups for both teams:Confirmed UCL lineups: FC Bayern Munich vs. Atalanta BergamoFC Bayern (4-2-3-1):Urbig - Stanišić, Kim, Tah, Guerreiro - Pavlović, Goretzka - Karl, Bischof, Díaz - KaneAtalanta Bergamo (3-4-2-1):Sportiello - Kossounou, Hien, Scalvini - Bellanova, Éderson, Pašalić, Bernasconi - De Ketelaere, Sulemana - ScamaccaWorld Cup playoffs updates: Race to fill final 6 spots startsFive talking points ahead of European World Cup playoffs77 days to the World Cup: Batistuta and the June 21 magic2026 World Cup playoffs explained: 6 spots up for grabsAdvertisementTerms and Privacy PolicyYour Privacy ChoicesAbout Our AdsAdvertisementAdvertisementStory byMUNICH, GERMANY - MARCH 18: Tom Bischof of FC Bayern Munich in action during the UEFA Champions League 2025/26 Round of 16 Second Leg match between FC Bayern München and Atalanta BC at Football Arena Munich on March 18, 2026 in Munich, Germany. (Photo by Stuart Franklin/Getty Images) | Getty ImagesCSmith1919Tue, March 24, 2026 at 5:30 PM UTC·1 min readGerman U-21 national team coach Antonio Di Salvo announced that Bayern Munich midfielder (though, he does not often play that position these days) Tom Bischof will captain the squad.“Tom will be our captain. He has done an outstanding job. I felt in our discussions that he was really keen to play these matches, and that he wanted to lead by example. He will also play in midfield and not out wide,” Germany U-21 coach Antonio Di Salvo (as captured by @iMiaSanMia).AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementBischof is in a weird spot — he is one of Germany’s best midfielders, but did not earn a call to the senior team because he rarely plays the position for Bayern Munich. On mostly any other team in the Bundesliga (including if he had stayed at Hoffenheim), Bischof likely would be starting and have earned a position under Julian Nagelsmann. The 20-year-old was already tracking in that direction, but Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany has mostly used Bischof out of position as an outside-back where he is not as good.Bischof was last called to Germany’s first team last May.If you are looking for more Bayern Munich and German national team coverage, check out the latest episodes of Bavarian Podcast Works, which you can get on Acast, Spotify, Apple, or any leading podcast distributor… Join the conversation!Sign up for a user account and get:New, improved notifications system!Fewer adsCreate community postsComment on articles, community postsRec comments, community postsAdvertisementAdvertisementAbout Our AdsAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisement",
